## Case text (Ask-CK ck.db zephyr_cases, key AWPTCM-T47210)
Title: MAC/Phy TLV with combination of user defined speed, duplex and auto nego
Objective / Precondition / Steps: (all empty in ck.db -- no step text, no expected result). Method applied (triage 2026-10-21, agreed):
enable the IEEE 802.3 MAC/PHY Configuration/Status TLV on both ends (`lldp tlv-select mac-phy-config` on x230 port1.0.1 and on AR4050S
port1.0.2), then put the DUT's port through nine speed/duplex/autoneg combinations and DECODE THE DUT'S TLV AT THE AR4050S
(`show lldp neighbors detail` on port1.0.2: Auto-negotiation Supported/Enabled|Disabled, Advertised Capability, Operational MAU Type).
Expected (IEEE 802.1AB / 802.3 subtype 1): autoneg Enabled with the advertised set equal to what `speed auto <n>` (+ duplex) allows, and
MAU = the negotiated mode, when autonegotiation is on; autoneg Disabled, advertised [none], MAU = the forced mode, when a fixed speed is set.
The forced rows (C4-C7) have the AR4050S matched so the link is up. The reverse direction (the x230's decode of the 4050's TLV) is read as
a bonus at C4-C7. Expected-output table from the 2026-10-09 run: tb470/x230v2-28GS/ports-2026-10-09T0845/47210/47210-review.md.

## Method / tools
tools/tb ckcon tb470 pp1323 <uN> 115200 ... with `@poll <s> <regex> <cmd>` (1.2 s per read; `do show ...` from config-if). For the
autonegotiation rows C2/C3/C9/C8 a watcher on u0 (47210-u0b.out, run in the background) polled `show lldp neighbors detail` for each row's
expected MAU in order while the DUT (47210-u1b.out) held each row for 12 s; the forced rows were done one console call at a time.
Files (verbatim below): 47210-u1a (DUT setup: tlv-select, show lldp local-info, HEALTH BEFORE, running-config after setup), 47210-u0a (4050
setup: tlv-select, running-config after setup, C1 baseline TLV), 47210-u0b (watcher: C2, C3, C9, C8 at the 4050), 47210-u1b (DUT rows
C2, C3, C9, C8), 47210-u1c4/u0c4 (C4), u1c5/u0c5 (C5), u1c6/u0c6 (C6), u1c7/u0c7 (C7), 47210-u1r (DUT: 4050's C7 TLV, then no speed /
no duplex), 47210-u0r (4050: no speed / no duplex, link a-1000, final TLV read, no lldp tlv-select, running-config, boot, reboot history,
exception log), 47210-u1t (DUT: no lldp tlv-select, final status/LLDP, HEALTH AFTER, running-config, boot).
.cfg files after setup, before step 1: swi_f.cfg from 47210-u1a.out (14:17:xx), swi_e.cfg from 47210-u0a.out (14:18:xx); both carry the
`lldp tlv-select mac-phy-config` line under the test port. HH:MM:SS >>> stamps are the box's clock (NZDT); DUT log lines are UTC.

## RESULT TABLE (the DUT's TLV as decoded at the AR4050S; every row from the files below)
| combo | DUT config (x230 port1.0.1) | 4050 port1.0.2 config | x230 status | 4050 status | Auto-negotiation | Advertised Capability | Operational MAU Type |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| C1 | auto (no speed, no duplex) | auto | a-full a-1000 | a-full a-1000 | Supported, Enabled | 1000BaseTFD, 100BaseTXFD, 100BaseTX, 10BaseTFD, 10BaseT | 1000BaseTFD (30) |
| C2 | speed auto 100 | auto | a-full a-100 | a-full a-100 | Supported, Enabled | 100BaseTXFD, 100BaseTX | 100BaseTXFD (16) |
| C3 | speed auto 100 + duplex half | auto | half a-100 | a-half a-100 | Supported, Enabled | 100BaseTX | 100BaseTXHD (15) |
| C9 | speed auto 10 (no duplex) | auto | a-full a-10 | a-full a-10 | Supported, Enabled | 10BaseTFD, 10BaseT | 10BaseTFD (11) |
| C8 | speed 1000 + duplex full | auto | full 1000 | a-full a-1000 | Supported, Disabled | [none] | 1000BaseTFD (30) |
| C4 | speed 100 + duplex full | speed 100 + duplex full | full 100 | full 100 | Supported, Disabled | [none] | 100BaseTXFD (16) |
| C5 | speed 100 + duplex half | speed 100 + duplex half | half 100 | half 100 | Supported, Disabled | [none] | 100BaseTXHD (15) |
| C6 | speed 10 + duplex full | speed 10 + duplex full | full 10 | full 10 | Supported, Disabled | [none] | 10BaseTFD (11) |
| C7 | speed 10 + duplex half | speed 10 + duplex half | half 10 | half 10 | Supported, Disabled | [none] | 10BaseTHD (10) |
| restore | no speed, no duplex | no speed, no duplex | a-full a-1000 | a-full a-1000 | Supported, Enabled | full set as C1 | 1000BaseTFD (30) |
Every row matches the 2026-10-09 expected table. The TLV was at the 4050 within one read (1.2-1.4 s) of the link settling in every forced
row; in the watcher rows it was seen 16-18 s after the DUT command (the watcher's poll cadence, not the device). Reverse direction (the
4050's TLV decoded at the x230) at C4/C5/C6/C7: Disabled / [none] / 16, 15, 11, 10 respectively (47210-u1c5/u1c6/u1c7/u1r).
No "% " line from either unit in any call.
Noted, not graded (same as 2026-10-09, platforms/x230v2-28GS.md §2): with a fixed `speed 1000` (C8) the DUT advertises autoneg "Disabled"
and [none] while the link still negotiates 1000/full with the partner at auto (1000BASE-T always uses clause-40 autoneg for master/slave);
the TLV reports the configured state. Left to the case owner.


